On another note, here's a semi-related concept: "Titles". Essentially 
you can only get one of these per game and only upon finishing the 
quest; there are 2 per class, and they are class-dependent. If you 
fulfill both sets of requirements, the title you get will be random.

#chatting to your quest leader should give hints about the requirements 
for each of these. I haven't made all of them up yet, but here's what I 
can think of.

ARCHAEOLOGIST:

Name: Daredevil
Reqs: Escape any of the following traps 50 times in total - falling 
rocks, boulders, spiked pits, polymorph traps - while wearing a fedora. 
Does not apply to boulder traps which have been "defused".
Rews: Increases your chances of escaping any trap.

Name: Professor of Archaeology
Reqs: Bring 6 identified artifacts to your quest home level and #chat 
with Lord Carnarvon. (He will take the artifacts from you.)
Rews: Gives you a blessed spellbook of identify, and increases your 
chance of casting it successfully by a flat 50%.

BARBARIAN:
?

CAVEFOO:
?

HEALER:

Name: Brain Surgeon
Reqs: Have maximum DEX when you complete the quest.
Rews: Gain double bonuses from eating MF corpses, and a 50% chance of 
resisting MF attacks (over and above the standard probabilities).

Name: ?

KNIGHT:

Name: Dragonlancer
Reqs: Successfully joust Ds or Js 20 times, while yourself mounted on a 
dragon.
Rews: Allows you to use the #monster command when mounted on a dragon 
(decreases your mount's Pw), and prevents your lance from breaking when 
jousting on dragonback. (Yes, I know NHINDND, but this is just too cool 
to pass up. :D)

Name: Crusader
Reqs: Kill the priest(ess) of Moloch in the Valley without donating to 
him/her. If the priest(ess) of Minetown is non-coaligned, you must also 
kill him/her without donating, and convert the Minetown altar.
Rews: +1d10 damage vs. demons and non-coaligned priests (includes the 
high priest of Moloch). Your alignment becomes "pious" immediately. If 
you killed the Minetown priest, you gain 3 points of divine protection. 
However, you can no longer wear a HoOA for any reason; if you try to, 
the helm crumbles to dust and you get 2 points of divine anger.

MONK:
?

PRIEST(ESS):

Name: Missionary
Reqs: Convert every last non-coaligned altar in the main dungeons and 
mines, before completing the quest. You must have visited all the levels 
above Medusa (can altars appear between Medusa and Castle?), except for 
Ludios and Sokoban, to qualify.
Rews: Allows you to convert the altar in the Valley of the Dead. (If you 
"would be converted", instead you get instant wide-angle disintegration; 
good luck.) Gives you a 50% chance of praying successfully in Gehennom. 
However, encounters with foocubi from now on (assuming the foocubus 
successfully removes your clothing) ALWAYS end with a negative effect, 
and ALWAYS auto-cancel the foocubus. ("The <foocubus> is disappointed by 
your lack of variety.")

Name: Vampire Hunter
Reqs: Kill 10 vampires, including at least 1 vampire lord.
Rews: Holy/unholy water does double damage. You get a +1 attack bonus 
when wielding a blessed weapon, and a 50% chance of resisting any curse 
attack.

RANGER:

Name: Airborne Ranger (heh)
Reqs: Kill Scorpius and at least 1 wumpus while levitating.
Rews: Grants intrinsic teleport control. If not an elf, grants intrinsic 
stealth or infravision (50/50 chance).

Name: Friend of the Forest
Reqs: Tame at least 3 different kinds of non-domestic, non-magical 
creatures, and keep them alive until you finish the quest.
Rews: Allows you to tame ALL non-magical creatures (includes 
brontotheria, mumakil, etc) by throwing food.

ROGUE:

Name: Stealth Assassin
Reqs: Kill at least 50 sleeping monsters, while invisible AND stealthy, 
before you finish the quest. The kill must be a "one-hit" one - i.e. no 
waking the monster up.
Rews: You gain +1d6 damage (versus monsters which cannot see you) when 
invisible and stealthy.

Name: Robber Baron
Reqs: Before finishing the quest, polymorph into a leprechaun or nymph 
and successfully steal from at least 10 monsters. OR successfully rob 2 
shops without using a pet (i.e. get the shopkeeper angry).
Rews: Whenever you attack in melee with at least one hand free (i.e. 
wielding a 1-handed weapon or barehanded, no shield, no #twoweapon), you 
have a 5% chance of stealing money and a 5% chance of stealing an item 
from the target.

SAMURAI:

Name: Battousai (heh)
Reqs: Kill 50 monsters of size Small or larger in a single melee attack 
with an edged weapon each.
Rews: +1d6 damage to any monster with full HP when wielding any sword, 
scimitar or saber; +1d10 instead if the weapon is a tsurugi or a katana. 
Does not apply when #twoweaponing or wearing a shield.

Name: Paragon of Bushido
Reqs: Never perform any action which would break EITHER the Samurai or 
Knight codes (until you finish the quest).
Rews: Decreases your prayer timeout by random(300) whenever you 
successfully pray. If you are crowned and successfully pray, the timeout 
penalty for being crowned is halved. However, you must now follow the 
Knight code or suffer the usual alignment penalty, and you get 1 point 
of divine anger every time you attack a peaceful monster.

TOURIST:

Name: Sightseer
Reqs: Take pictures of any 4 of the following: statue of Perseus, statue 
of a centaur, named demon, Vlad, Rodney, Kroisos, the treasure zoo in 
Sokoban, or any part of Mines' End.
Rews: Never forget a level layout, even when hit by a MF attack. When 
taking pictures with your camera, there is a 1 in 3 chance that the 
monster will become peaceful instead of blinded (as scroll of taming, 
but without the possibility of actually taming the monster).

Name: Souvenir Hunter
Reqs: Buy something from EVERY shop in the Dungeons of Doom and 
Minetown, never anger any shopkeepers, and never sell any items (until 
you get the title). You must have visited all the levels above Medusa 
(can shops appear between Medusa and Castle?), except for Sokoban and 
Ludios, to qualify.
Rews: Allows you to use artifacts regardless of alignment (but class 
restrictions still apply).

VALKYRIE:

Name: Odin's Right Hand
Reqs: Tame 2 ravens and keep them alive until you finish the Quest.
Rews: If lawful, after finishing the Quest you automatically convert to 
neutral (as does your Quest Leader). Gain +2 to INT and WIS, and +1 to 
your maximum INT and WIS; your pet ravens gain 5 levels each. If the 
ravens die, they "vanish" instead.

Name: Soulbringer
Reqs: Destroy 30 ghosts.
Rews: Gives you the Knight ability to mount creatures without decreasing 
their tameness. When mounted on a horse, allows it to levitate at will. 
Gives you a blessed saddle (but find your own horse!).

WIZARD:

Name: Necromancer
Reqs: Successfully turn undead on 20 different corpses.
Rews: Flat 50% bonus to taming all undead. Undead pets will not lose 
tameness when you are on a different level.

Name: ?

